.TH ASK-QUOTA 1 "2026-08-14" "ask-quota" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
ask\-quota \- see which tasks consumed your Claude Code quota
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ask\-quota
.RI [ window ]
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B ask\-quota
reads the Claude Code transcripts stored under
.I ~/.claude/projects
and reports which sessions consumed the current quota window.
.PP
Quota tools report how much is left. This one reports where it went.
.PP
Rows are ranked by a cost weight derived from published price ratios: cache
reads count for a tenth of an input token, cache writes for one and a quarter,
and output tokens for five. The weight is a ranking device, not a price: it
deliberately ignores the differences between models.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-window " name"
Window to report on:
.BR 5h " (default), " week ", or " 30d .
May also be given as the first positional argument, so
.B ask\-quota week
works.
.TP
.BI \-\-top " n"
How many rows to show. Accepts a positive number or
.BR all .
Default is 5.
.TP
.BI \-\-group\-by " mode"
.B session
(default) shows one row per session.
.B project
merges every session that ran in the same directory, which is how one feature
worked across several repositories reads as a single number.
.TP
.B \-\-json
Print rows as a JSON array for piping. No header line, no formatting: token
counts are exact rather than abbreviated.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print the version and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-help
Print a short usage summary and exit.
.SH WINDOWS
The 5-hour and 7-day windows match the ones the service itself enforces. When
an external quota source is installed, their boundaries are read from it. When
none is present,
.B ask\-quota
infers the current 5-hour block from the transcripts themselves: a block opens
on a message and closes five hours later, so the current block begins at the
first message after the previous one closed. Measured against a live window,
this inference landed within nine minutes.
.PP
The 30-day window has no upstream equivalent. It is always the last 30 days,
and it never carries an official percentage.
.SH COLUMNS
.TP
.B SHARE
This row's percentage of the window's total cost. Fully measured from local
data; shares always sum to 100%.
.TP
.B QUOTA
SHARE scaled by the officially reported percentage used, estimating how many
points of the real quota window this row accounts for. This is a proportion,
not a measurement, and it appears only when an official figure is available.
.TP
.BR OUT ", " CACHE_W ", " CACHE_R
Output, cache-write and cache-read tokens, abbreviated.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
.B ask\-quota
The top five sessions of the current 5-hour block.
.TP
.B ask\-quota week \-\-group\-by project
Which repositories consumed this week's quota.
.TP
.B ask\-quota 30d \-\-top all \-\-json | jq
Every session of the last 30 days, machine-readable.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success, including the case where no usage was found.
.TP
.B 2
Invalid arguments.
.SH LIMITATIONS
Only transcripts on this machine are visible. Sessions run on another machine,
in the web application, or by cloud agents consume the same quota but leave no
local trace, so they cannot appear in this report. A number here is therefore a
breakdown of local work, not necessarily of everything the account consumed.
.PP
The cost weight ignores per-model price differences, so rows are ranked
consistently but not priced.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.claude/projects
Transcript directory, one subdirectory per working directory.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR jq (1)
